WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.752
I think it's so interesting
what you were saying earlier--

00:00:02.752 --> 00:00:06.464
as a person who's been blind
your whole life-- not seeing

00:00:06.464 --> 00:00:12.679
color, but also feeling and
recognizing the racial

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:18.893
injustices and how people-- all
of us who are seeing-- judge

00:00:18.893 --> 00:00:22.230
each other by the color of our
skin. It must be very

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:27.694
interesting as a blind man for
race to play such a major role

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:32.615
in this country when for you it
truly isn't an issue 'cause you

00:00:32.615 --> 00:00:35.660
--you can honestly say you
don't see color.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:40.540
No--well, I do see color, but I
don't see it like that. I see

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.419
color in the spirit of the
person. And your spirit is

00:00:44.419 --> 00:00:51.509
either good or bad. That's the
bottom line. You are living for

00:00:51.509 --> 00:00:55.805
the perpetuation of life or you
are actually killing yourself

00:00:55.805 --> 00:00:59.434
with the hate you have within.
That's what's up.

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:03.855
Okay, so where you sit now--
and you are, I know, a deeply

00:01:03.855 --> 00:01:08.318
spiritual person, not just
religious, but a deeply

00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:12.447
spiritual, feeling, conscious
person-- what do you think of

00:01:12.447 --> 00:01:15.533
where we are as humanity and
how we're doing?

00:01:18.703 --> 00:01:21.748
I think that people have gotten
so hung up in what they see

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:26.252
online, and, you know,
everyone's perpetuating hate

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:31.716
as opposed to love, and, you
know, it's a heartbreak for me,

00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:37.514
it really is, because I think
you know, we have far much more

00:01:37.514 --> 00:01:42.143
potential as human beings than
we're giving ourselves.

00:01:42.143 --> 00:01:44.604
We're destroying the planet and
saying, "Oh, that's not real."

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:49.859
I--I don't know what people are thinking
about. You know, you are not

00:01:49.859 --> 00:01:55.323
really privileged. Because when
you take from the almighty that

00:01:55.323 --> 00:01:59.577
has given everything to you for
absolutely free and begin to

00:01:59.577 --> 00:02:01.830
feel like, "Hey, well, that's--
"that's what I'm supposed to

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:05.083
have, this is how it's supposed
to be, and just for me,"

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:09.629
well, then, that's the
beginning of your death.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:12.298
You know, you wrapped up your
video when you were speaking

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:15.885
about what was going on in the
world with an urgent plea.

00:02:15.885 --> 00:02:19.430
In the words of John Lewis, you
were saying, "Do good trouble,"

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.225
and for me, good trouble is
bringing our nation,

00:02:22.225 --> 00:02:24.102
this nation, back together
again. Together.

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:27.647
Yeah, and the way we do that is
to vote justice in and

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:30.483
injustice out, so--
Out.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:35.280
Out. What do you wanna say-- I
am just sort of-- I'm baffled

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:40.535
by anyone who believes with the
state of our nation that their

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:43.163
vote doesn't matter. What do
you wanna say about that? When,

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:48.376
you know, you and I, in the
same age range, came up in a

00:02:48.376 --> 00:02:51.754
generation where, you know,
people still were fighting for

00:02:51.754 --> 00:02:53.381
the right to vote.

00:02:53.381 --> 00:03:03.099
Listen, when you have a group
of people who actually plan to

00:03:03.099 --> 00:03:07.979
kidnap a governor of a state...
Mm.

00:03:07.979 --> 00:03:12.192
Because they feel a certain
kind of way, we are completely

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:14.485
off-beat.
Yeah.

00:03:14.485 --> 00:03:17.238
You know, can you-- would you
share what you're trying to do

00:03:17.238 --> 00:03:19.449
with the god that you
say you serve? Would you do

00:03:19.449 --> 00:03:24.621
that? Would the god you serve
feel good about that from you?

00:03:27.081 --> 00:03:31.920
It's bull tish.
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:38.468
It really is. And so I just
feel that we have to... we have

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:45.350
to vote, you know, injustice
out and positive in.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:49.604
So along with all the hundreds
of songs that you have written

00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:52.357
for yourself, you've written
'em for other people. 

00:03:52.357 --> 00:03:56.819
We watched you earlier in the
year in that great special when

00:03:56.819 --> 00:04:00.073
you were with Alicia Keys and
everybody and you played "Lean

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:03.618
On Me." what do you think we
can be leaning on right now?

00:04:03.618 --> 00:04:07.413
What should we be leaning on?
Everybody loves that song.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:13.878
Lean on the goodness in your
heart. Lean on that. Lean on--lean on

00:04:13.878 --> 00:04:20.385
knowing that how you do today
will affect what will happen

00:04:20.385 --> 00:04:25.056
to your children and their
children, and so forth on--

00:04:25.056 --> 00:04:29.352
tomorrow. Lean on the fact that
you have to speak

00:04:29.352 --> 00:04:31.437
and not be afraid.

